SHA256SUMS records each source and license checksum. Regeneration verifies
these files and needs no network connection or external source checkout.
The newer descriptor.proto defines debug_redact, which the descriptor.proto
bundled with grpc-tools 1.13.1 does not define. The API source is not patched.

Run npm ci, then scripts/generate-substrate.sh. Use --check to compare the
result with src/substrate/generated without changing the generated files.
The generator uses ts-proto 2.18.4 and grpc-tools 1.13.1 (protoc 3.19.1).
It generates grpc-js services, bigint int64 fields, .js ESM imports, and
Timestamp messages with seconds and nanos. It does not generate JSON helpers.
The generated code requires @grpc/grpc-js and @bufbuild/protobuf at runtime.
The generated files are derived sources. Do not edit them manually.

The loopback gRPC tests verify the generated transport contract only.
They do not establish platform authentication, authorization, credential
rotation, snapshot creation, or remote durability.
